## ARCHITECTURE.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
**Read when**: Any structural change, new layers, mappers, or error flow
**Reglas criticas**:
1. Presentation NEVER imports URLSession, DTOs, SwiftData, or JSON parsing
2. Domain models MUST be pure — no framework imports
3. Data layer MUST map DTOs to Domain models via Mappers
4. DecoratorMappers transform Domain → Decorator (presentation models)
5. Repository protocol lives in Domain; Data holds only the Impl

## PROJECT-STRUCTURE.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/PROJECT-STRUCTURE.md
**Read when**: Creating new files, deciding where each file goes
**Reglas criticas**:
1. Domain/ and Data/ are GLOBAL layers (not inside Features/)
2. Features/ contains ONLY presentation: DI, UI, Presentation, Navigation
3. Core/ contains shared infrastructure: DesignSystem, Networking, Persistence, Common
4. MUST follow exact folder hierarchy per feature

## new-feature.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/new-feature.md
**Read when**: Creating a new feature (complete checklist)
**Reglas criticas**:
1. MUST create files in three separate locations: Domain/, Data/, Features/
2. MUST decide routes, states, errors, and data sources before coding
3. MUST follow exact naming convention: [Feature]Model, [Feature]UseCase, etc.
4. MUST create Factory in Features/[Feature]/DI/

## swiftui-code-style.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/swiftui-code-style.md
**Read when**: Creating/modifying Views or ViewModels
**Reglas criticas**:
1. MUST organize files: imports → MARK → properties → init → body → private → extension → previews
2. MUST use // MARK: - for every section
3. MUST keep body small — extract to private subviews/helpers
4. Custom ViewModifiers MUST go in Core/Common/SwiftUI/Modifiers/

## design-system.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/design-system.md
**Read when**: Creating/modifying UI, colors, typography, accessibility
**Reglas criticas**:
1. MUST use semantic colors (Color(.systemBackground)), NEVER hardcoded Color.black/white
2. MUST support Dynamic Type — NEVER use fixed font sizes
3. MUST use system colors for accents (Color(.systemBlue))
4. MUST test both Light and Dark Mode

## swift-concurrency.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/swift-concurrency.md
**Read when**: Async/await code, actors, Sendable, Task, Swift 6
**Reglas criticas**:
1. MUST make Domain Models, DTOs, UseCases, Repositories, Mappers Sendable
2. ViewModels MUST NOT be Sendable (already @MainActor isolated)
3. NEVER pass SwiftData models between actors — pass IDs
4. MUST propagate CancellationError, NEVER swallow it

## swiftdata.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/swiftdata.md
**Read when**: Persistence, ModelContainer, ModelExecutor, migrations
**Reglas criticas**:
1. SwiftData MUST only be in Data layer — NEVER in Domain or Presentation
2. Each repository MUST use its own ModelExecutor, NEVER the main ModelContext
3. MUST use ModelContainer.shared in production and an in-memory container in previews and tests
4. MUST map SwiftData models to Domain models, NEVER expose SD models

## networking.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/networking.md
**Read when**: Creating/modifying endpoints, APIClient, interceptors
**Reglas criticas**:
1. MUST use dual-endpoint system: Endpoint (internal) vs APIEndpoint (external)
2. APIClient protocol MUST be Sendable
3. MUST handle errors with typed APIError, NEVER swallow with try?
4. APIClientImpl is final class (not struct) — holds URLSession reference

## testing.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/testing.md
**Read when**: Writing unit tests, mocks, or test stubs
**Reglas criticas**:
1. MUST use Swift Testing (import Testing), NEVER XCTest for new tests
2. High priority: UseCase, ViewModel (state transitions), Error Mappers
3. MUST mirror source structure in test folder: Tests/Domain, Tests/Data, Tests/Features
4. MUST create Mock types in Tests/Mocks/ folder

## security-privacy.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/security-privacy.md
**Read when**: Privacy Manifests, Keychain, secure storage
**Reglas criticas**:
1. MUST include PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy for App Store (iOS 17+)
2. NEVER store secrets in UserDefaults or @AppStorage — use Keychain
3. MUST declare Required Reason APIs in Privacy Manifest
4. NEVER log sensitive data (tokens, passwords, PII)

## ui-testing.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/ui-testing.md
**Read when**: Accessibility identifiers, UI test data, Page Objects, UI tests
**Reglas criticas**:
1. MUST locate elements by accessibility identifier, NEVER by label
2. Test data MUST enter through the Factory (stub or fixture data sources), NEVER by changing ViewModels or Views
3. NEVER use sleep() — wait on conditions
4. UI tests use XCTest; unit tests use Swift Testing

## tooling.md
**Path**: .claude/docs/tooling.md
**Read when**: Building, running tests, checking the app in the simulator, crashes, profiling
**Reglas criticas**:
1. Build and test through axbuild when it is installed
2. ALWAYS pass an explicit simulator UDID, NEVER `booted`
3. Verify the effect of a UI action, NEVER the tap itself

